  "content": {
    "title": "Florida gymnastics wins SEC Championship with top bars score of 2026 season",
    "text": "March 21, 2026Updated March 22, 2026, 1:49 a.m. ETThe Florida Gators gymnastics team won its first SEC Championship in three years.Florida narrowly defeated Oklahoma by a score of 198.175 to 198.150.The Gators secured the victory with a phenomenal 49.800 score on the uneven bars in the final rotation.Selena Harris-Miranda scored a perfect 10 on the uneven bars during the championship meet.Riley McCusker and Florida gymnastics waited anxiously to see if the Gators were right.For much of the season, the squad thought it was the best in the SEC. Now, they waited to see if the judges agreed at the SEC Championship.By 0.025, UF showed the gymnastics world its belief was correct.Florida has peaked the last three meets of the season, and in Saturday’s SEC Championship, the Gators peaked when the meet mattered most with a phenomenal 49.800 on uneven bars.That was enough to upend mighty Oklahoma and LSU to win the program’s first SEC Championship in three years. The Gators finished with a 198.175 to just barely top Oklahoma’s 198.150. LSU came in third at 197.950 and Alabama in fourth at 197.475.UF hung around with the Sooners and Tigers for much of the meet, but it fell into third after a 49.425 on vault. Florida, though, ranks No. 1 in bars and needed all of its season-best score on the event to overcome the 49.600 the Sooners tallied on the floor.Skye Blakely and Kayla DiCello scored 9.975s on the bars, and Selena Harris-Miranda was pure perfection once again with a 10. Riley McCusker anchored with a 9.925.Here’s how it happened:Florida gymnastics at the SEC Championship live updates Rotation 4: Florida gymnastics (Bars) 49.800; 198.175The Gators truly save their best for last and deliver a bars showing for the ages in Tulsa to win the program's first SEC Championship in three years. It was near perfection for Skye Blakely and Kayla DiCello with 9.975s. Selena Harris-Miranda then made it complete perfection with a 10, and Riley McCusker's 9.925 to anchor was enough to clinch the title for the Gators by 0.025 over No. 1 Oklahoma and 0.225 over No. 2 LSU. Rotation 3: Florida gymnastics (Vault) 49.425; 148.375Gators fall into third on the vault as Harris-Miranda anchors with an uncharacterisly low 9.800. Florida still within striking distance. Anya Pilgrim and Blakely lead with a 9.900. Rotiation 2: Florida gymnastics (Floor) 49.425Gators score takes a slight step back from the last two star-studded weeks, but the squad still registers an impressive score. DiCello, Harris-Miranda and eMjae Frazier each score a 9.900. Rotation 1: Florida gymnastics (Beam) 49.525Gators put up a 49.525 on the beam, which is the fourth best for the team (Florida ranks No. 1 in beam score heading into the meet). Skye Blakely scores a 9.900, and Kayla DiCello and Selena Harris-Miranda end with a 9.950.Florida gymnastics at the SEC Championship starting lineupsVaultAnya Pilgrim, eMjae Frazier, Kayla DiCello, Danie Ferris, Skye Blakely, Selena Harris-MirandaBarsFrazier, Pilgrim, Blakely, DiCello, Harris-Miranda, Riley McCuskerBeamSkylar Draser, Alyssa Arana, Blakely, Frazier, DiCello, Harris-MirandaFloorGabby Disidore, Ferris, Frazier, DiCello, Blakely, Harris-MirandaWhat channel is Florida gymnastics at the SEC Championship?TV Channel: SEC NetworkStreaming: ESPN.com or the ESPN AppThe SEC Championships will be broadcast on the SEC Network. Olympians Samantha Peszek, Aly Raisman and John Roethlisberger calling the action and Taylor Davis providing sideline reports.What time is Florida gymnastics at the SEC Championship?Date: Saturday, March 21Start time: 8 p.m. ETThe Gators will compete as part of the evening session with the other top three-rankedNoah Ram covers Florida Gators athletics and Gainesville-area high school sports for The Gainesville Sun, GatorSports.com and the USA TODAY Network. Contact him at nram@usatodayco.com. Follow him on X @Noah_ram1 and on Instagram @Ramreporter. Read his coverage of the Gators’ national championship basketball season in “CHOMP-IONS!” — a hardcover coffee-table collector’s book from The Sun. Details at Florida.ChampsBook.com.",
